   "notes": "Botany Building (W.S. Weatherley, 1904), south range: red-brown brick with buff stone bands and dressings, three main storeys of regular sash/cross windows and a slate mansard with a row of small dormers. The 2019 Mapillary views (one stationary car, raking from the south-west) show it under scaffolding, so the window grid (10 bays) and dormer count (8) are estimated; materials also follow the Commons photo of the courtyard (north) front."
